    "assumptions": [
      "Materials-only on-time feasibility: complete BOM available by the customer deadline. Production duration, factory capacity, weekends and transport costs are not scheduled.",
      "Orders sort by earliest deadline, higher numeric priority, then lexical order ID. Allocation is all-or-nothing; failed orders reserve no inventory.",
      "Stock is available as of the request date. Receipts are consumed oldest-arrival first and only if arrival is on or before the order deadline; quantities are globally conserved.",
      "A PLANNED dispatch in [outage_start, outage_end_exclusive) moves to the exclusive end, preserving its documented transit interval. DISPATCHED and CANCELLED facts are not shifted.",
      "Existing booked receipts are committed facts. Outage backlog dispatch smoothing and revalidation of historical procurement certificates are not modeled.",
      "New proposals start no earlier than as_of, use per-part shipping capacity after booked dispatches, and arrive dispatch + lead_days. All required certificates must cover arrival.",
      "The provided inbound schedule is treated as exhaustive only for parts with shipment records or an explicit inbound_schedule_complete flag. Missing vital facts are unresolved.",
      "Mitigation is a bounded greedy heuristic, not a proven global optimum. Compare mixed cost-first, mixed lead-first and single-supplier policies. Maximize restored newly-at-risk orders, minimize unused new units, then gross additional cost, then stable supplier IDs. Plans cannot make an already on-time disrupted order worse.",
      "The additional-procurement search horizon is capped at 366 calendar days from as_of.",
      "Gross additional procurement cost is new proposed quantity times graph unit cost, rounded per shipment to 2 decimals with ROUND_HALF_UP. Cancellation fees, sunk commitments, labor, taxes and transport are excluded. Proposals are not persisted or placed.",
      "A comparison may indirectly change unrelated order allocation through shared stock. Direct dependency paths and newly-at-risk status are reported separately."
